      "hints": [
        "Angle $OAB$ has vertex $A$: use $\\overrightarrow{AO}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ (or reverse both).",
        "Calculate the dot product and both lengths before inverse cosine."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "$\\overrightarrow{BA}=\\overrightarrow{OA}-\\overrightarrow{OB}=(-5,-1,2)$; using $\\overrightarrow{OA}$ and $\\overrightarrow{BA}$ reverses both rays from $A$.",
        "$\\overrightarrow{OA}\\cdot\\overrightarrow{BA}=2(-5)+3(-1)+5(2)=-3$; $|OA|=\\sqrt{38}$ and $|BA|=\\sqrt{30}$.",
        "$\\cos\\angle OAB=-\\frac3{\\sqrt{38}\\sqrt{30}}$, so $\\angle OAB=95.1^\\circ$ (3 s.f.)."
      ],
